{"id": "EUVD-2026-101135", "enisaUuid": "1b9dd34b-bca2-39ad-9181-a0d887e650b1", "description": "libsmb2 through 6.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in smb2_decode_file_all_info that allows malicious SMB servers to crash clients by sending an unchecked FileNameLength. Attackers controlling the server or performing man-in-the-middle on unsigned sessions can return crafted FileAllInformation replies to smb2_stat or smb2_fstat calls, crashing the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:40:05", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libsmb2-query-info-reply-oob-read", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/blob/d67e213a5c4e7e4969fd81f0b95e4ca5831fbba1/lib/smb2-data-file-info.c#L202", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/commit/57bee9fb941a39307145b82e4dd1718862f30a74", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsmb2-through-6.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-smb2-decode-file-all-info"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r4h5-4wv2-c8cj", "CVE-2026-110712"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "834e83b7-703c-327a-b1db-9d6c55c64e73", "product": {"name": "libsmb2", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d0a55c49-7aaa-3cda-8b73-4a9787c2b9fd", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}], "isExploited": false}